WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.960
A galaxy you can see for yourself.

00:02.734 --> 00:08.007
Andromeda, the nearest large galaxy to our own, two and a half million light-years off.

00:08.453 --> 00:11.833
You can see it without any telescope, as a faint smudge.

00:12.466 --> 00:16.923
How well you see it, like everything on this trip, depends on how dark your sky is.
